      "text": "To convert from spherical coordinates $\\left( \\rho, \\theta, \\phi \\right)$ to rectangular coordinates $\\left( x, y, z \\right)$, we use the following equations:\n\n1. $x = \\rho \\sin{\\phi} \\cos{\\theta}$\n2. $y = \\rho \\sin{\\phi} \\sin{\\theta}$\n3. $z = \\rho \\cos{\\phi}$\n\nFor the given point $\\left( 3, \\frac{5 \\pi}{12}, 0 \\right)$, we have:\n\n1. $x = 3 \\sin{0} \\cos{\\left(\\frac{5 \\pi}{12}\\right)}$\n2. $y = 3 \\sin{0} \\sin{\\left(\\frac{5 \\pi}{12}\\right)}$\n3. $z = 3 \\cos{0}$\n\nSince $\\sin{0} = 0$, equation 1 simplifies to $x = 0$. Equations 2 and 3 simplify to $y = 0$ and $z = 3$ respectively.\n\nSo the rectangular coordinates are $\\boxed{(0, 0, 3)}$.",
