      "text": "To convert from spherical coordinates to rectangular coordinates, we use the following conversion formulas:\n\n$x = \\rho \\sin(\\phi) \\cos(\\theta)$\n\n$y = \\rho \\sin(\\phi) \\sin(\\theta)$\n\n$z = \\rho \\cos(\\phi)$\n\nGiven the spherical coordinates $\\rho = 3$, $\\theta = \\frac{5 \\pi}{12}$, and $\\phi = 0$, we can compute the rectangular coordinates as follows:\n\n$ x = 3 \\sin(0) \\cos\\left(\\frac{5 \\pi}{12}\\right) = 0$\n\n$ y = 3 \\sin(0) \\sin\\left(\\frac{5 \\pi}{12}\\right) = 0$\n\n$ z = 3 \\cos(0) = 3$\n\nTherefore, the rectangular coordinates corresponding to the spherical coordinates $\\left( x, y, z \\right) = (0, 0, 3)$ are:\n\n$\\boxed{(0, 0, 3)}$",
